{
  "name": "How to Measure for a New Pull-Out Cabinet Shelf",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Getting the right fit for your pull-out cabinet shelves starts with accurate measurements. It's not as simple as just guessing! First, clear out the cabinet completely so you have a clean slate. You'll need to measure the interior width, depth, and height of the cabinet opening. For the width, measure from inside wall to inside wall, making sure to account for any hinges or face frames that might protrude. For depth, measure from the back of the cabinet to the front, stopping before the cabinet door. Finally, measure the height from the bottom of the cabinet to any shelves or obstructions above. Remember to consider how much weight the shelf will carry and the type of slide extension you need. If your cabinet has uneven framing or tricky obstructions like plumbing, it can make the process much harder. In those cases, or if you're planning multiple units for a kitchen remodel across areas like Highlands Ranch or Castle Rock, bringing in a pro like HH Remodeling LLC can ensure everything aligns perfectly and functions smoothly.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
